  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Fiesta** (1 review): Fiesta closed the encore, leaving the crowd wanting more [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Please help my pony**: back after 81 archived shows (826 days); rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n- **Hammer**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2008-07-13.church** (recommended): source not stated; 30 songs; 133 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **ween2008-07-13**: source not stated; 30 songs; 129 min; rated 4.33/5 by 3 [2]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the audio sounds good so far, and calls the set relatively short but rocking [6]\n- **ween2008-07-13.core**: source not stated; 30 songs; 132 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer speculates Dean got very high during the show and couldn't play more, so the band left early after the final encore song [4]\n- Crossroads is an outdoor venue, considered one of Kansas City's best and likely the best for summer shows [6]\n- After the show, the connected bar stayed open past 3, and Ween played a couple more hours in a packed room [6]\n- Reviewer has seen many Ween shows; this one was good but notably short, with only three encore songs [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2008-07-13.church**: taped by Chris King; transferred by Chris King; source: Church-Audio STC-11> Church-Audio ST-9100 > M-audio2 (24/96) [1]\n- **ween2008-07-13**: taped by Snoof; transferred by Snoof; source: MBHO603a/ka200(DINa,ROC)>R4@24/44.1 [2]\n- **ween2008-07-13.core**: taped by Chris King; transferred by Chris King; source: Core Sound Mic Core In Line Pre amp > M-audio1 (24/96) [3]",
